    "body": "> Yes, I'm just not sure how that works on other platforms.\r\n\r\nWhich platform you have? If this works on a Mac (I tested it, it does) it will work on other BSDs. The only other case would be GNU `tar` which I believe is fully backward compatible with BSD implementation.\r\n\r\n> I guess another way to think of the question is this: can we think of a value of VERBOSE that will break the dashless form in a bad way (e.g. extracting the wrong file, passing inadvertent flags to tar) but won't break the dash form?\r\n\r\nWell, that is a really hard question to answer... I guess we are a bit safer with dashed form because anything before `-f` would be treated as a flag, assuming that bad flag is better than operating on a bad file...",
    "created_at": "2020-06-11T04:54:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T04:54:50Z",
